            "title": "How often should you clean a copper water bottle?",
            "icon": "shield_check",
            "use_product_description": false,
            "open_by_default": false,
            "content": "<p>Rinse it with warm water every day after the last sip and let it air-dry upside down with the cap off. Give it a lemon-and-salt clean every week or two, or whenever the copper darkens more than you like or you notice green spots.</p>"
          }
        },
