            "title": "Why does my water taste metallic?",
            "icon": "glass_water",
            "use_product_description": false,
            "open_by_default": false,
            "content": "<p>Some people notice a faint copper taste even in plain water. A clear metallic or bitter taste usually comes from an acidic or hot drink, water left too many hours, very soft or reverse-osmosis water, a bottle due for its lemon-and-salt clean, or a brand-new bottle.</p><p>Pour that water out and refill with plain still water. Do not keep the same water longer than 24 hours.</p>"
